From fe0316b58956c7e25a8eada82efca043dccf733a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 07:26:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Surface errors when external links
 (tel/WhatsApp/maps/web) fail to open
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

launchUrl() was called fire-and-forget everywhere it's used (Call,
WhatsApp, Directions on Business Details; Privacy/Terms/social links on
Settings and About Us) — on a device with no dialer, no WhatsApp
installed, or no browser/maps app, the button visibly did nothing, with
no way to tell it apart from a broken button. Added a shared
launchUrlSafely() helper (core/utils/url_launcher_helper.dart) that
awaits the result, logs failures, and shows an AppToast.error when the
link genuinely could not be opened.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UWLxdJ74EiJDqqczEM3fhE
