From 38a16176b714ca57cc2d815ff31674e4ce98e365 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 11:44:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Surface favorite-toggle failures instead of silently
 swallowing them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

FavoriteToggleController.toggleBusiness/toggleEvent discarded the
Either<Failure, void> result from ToggleFavoriteUseCase entirely, and
its AsyncValue<void> state was never watched anywhere (only .notifier
was ever read) — so a failed toggle (e.g. a Hive write error) left the
favorite icon looking like nothing happened, with no feedback at all.
Both methods now return the failure message (or null on success), and
every call site (Business Details, Event Details, Favorites screen)
shows an AppToast.error when it's non-null.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UWLxdJ74EiJDqqczEM3fhE
---
